   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Word Roller Countdown\n\nA countdown that scrolls through its numbers, then a blurred, accelerating spin that lands on a launch word with a springy settle.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A launch, reveal or sale start: 5 4 3 2 1 and then the big word.\n- A tense, high-energy moment before a title.\n\nAvoid when:\n- A calm title: the digits scroll and the screen pulses by design.\n- A real clock or date: use event-countdown-clock.\n\nVariables:\n- numbers (string): Countdown, default \"5, 4, 3, 2, 1\"\n- final_word (string): Final word, default \"LAUNCH\"\n- subtitle (string): Subtitle, default \"YOUR JOURNEY BEGINS\"\n- font_size (number, 40-500): Font size, default 180\n- color (color): Digit color, default \"#0a0a0a\"\n- accent (color): Launch color, default \"#2563eb\"\n- background (color): Background, default \"#fafafa\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/lifeprompt-team/remotion-scenes. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Word Roller Countdown\n\n  A countdown that scrolls through its numbers, then a blurred, accelerating spin that lands on a launch word with a springy settle.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/lifeprompt-team/remotion-scenes/blob/02c7a84241da7010b5f59c420b0110aafd1d6f0d/src/scenes/RollerAnimations/RollerCountdown.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 lifeprompt-team\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"word-roller-countdown\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"4\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"numbers\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Countdown\", \"description\": \"The values counted through, separated by commas.\", \"default\": \"5, 4, 3, 2, 1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"final_word\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Final word\", \"description\": \"Word shown after the spin.\", \"default\": \"LAUNCH\"},\n    {\"id\": \"subtitle\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Subtitle\", \"description\": \"Small caps line under the final word.\", \"default\": \"YOUR JOURNEY BEGINS\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Size of the countdown digits in pixels. The launch word shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 180, \"min\": 40, \"max\": 500, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Digit color\", \"description\": \"Color of the countdown digits.\", \"default\": \"#0a0a0a\"},\n    {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Launch color\", \"description\": \"Color of the final word.\", \"default\": \"#2563eb\"},\n    {\"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Background\", \"description\": \"Fill behind the text. Use transparent to lay the block over your own footage.\", \"default\": \"#fafafa\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"x\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Word Roller Countdown</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@100;300;400;500;600;700;800;900&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .wcd-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n\n        #root { color: var(--c, #0a0a0a); }\n        .wcd-g { position: relative; text-align: center; line-height: 1; }\n        .wcd-win { position: relative; height: 1em; overflow: hidden; }\n        .wcd-mask { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; height: 0.222em; z-index: 1; }\n        .wcd-mask.t { top: 0; }\n        .wcd-mask.b { bottom: 0; }\n        .wcd-num { height: 1em; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; padding: 0 0.3em; }\n        .wcd-fin { display: none; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ac, #2563eb); white-space: pre; }\n        .wcd-sub { display: none; font-size: 0.111em; color: #737373; margin-top: 1.5em; letter-spacing: 0.25em; white-space: pre; }\n        .wcd-probe { position: absolute; visibility: hidden; white-space: pre; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.667em; left: 0; top: 0; }\n\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"word-roller-countdown\" data-duration=\"4\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"wcd-clip\" class=\"wcd-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"4\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"wcd-g\" class=\"wcd-g\">\n            <div id=\"wcd-win\" class=\"wcd-win\">\n              <div id=\"wcd-mt\" class=\"wcd-mask t\"></div>\n              <div id=\"wcd-mb\" class=\"wcd-mask b\"></div>\n              <div id=\"wcd-sc\"><div id=\"wcd-n0\" class=\"wcd-num\"></div><div id=\"wcd-n1\" class=\"wcd-num\"></div></div>\n            </div>\n            <div id=\"wcd-fin\" class=\"wcd-fin\"></div>\n            <div id=\"wcd-sub\" class=\"wcd-sub\"></div>\n            <div id=\"wcd-probe\" class=\"wcd-probe\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function el(id) { return document.getElementById(id); }\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return value !== \"\" && value !== null && value !== undefined && Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function txt(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function list(value, fallback, max) {\n              var a = (typeof value === \"string\" ? value : \"\").split(\",\").map(function (s) { return s.trim(); }).filter(Boolean);\n              if (!a.length) a = fallback.slice();\n              return a.slice(0, max || 12);\n            }\n            function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 32; i++) {\n                  var u = 1 - t;\n                  var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                var v = 1 - t;\n                return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            var E = {\n              out: bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), \"in\": bezier(0.7, 0, 0.84, 0), inOut: bezier(0.87, 0, 0.13, 1),\n              overshoot: bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1), smooth: bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1),\n              quadIn: function (x) { return x * x; },\n              quadOut: function (x) { return 1 - (1 - x) * (1 - x); },\n              cubicOut: function (x) { return 1 - Math.pow(1 - x, 3); },\n              cubicInOut: function (x) { return x < 0.5 ? 4 * x * x * x : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * x + 2, 3) / 2; }\n            };\n            function clamp01(p) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p)); }\n            // the source framework interpolate with clamped ends, one input range and one output range.\n            function ip(x, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var p = b === a ? (x >= b ? 1 : 0) : clamp01((x - a) / (b - a));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(p) : p);\n            }\n            // Damped spring from 0 towards 1 (mass, stiffness, damping), frame at 30 fps, in closed form.\n            function spring(frame, cfg) {\n              if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n              var t = frame / 30, m = cfg.mass || 1, k = cfg.stiffness === undefined ? 100 : cfg.stiffness, c = cfg.damping === undefined ? 10 : cfg.damping;\n              var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / m), z = c / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * m));\n              if (Math.abs(z - 1) < 1e-6) return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n              if (z < 1) {\n                var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + (z * w0 / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n              }\n              var q = w0 * Math.sqrt(z * z - 1), r1 = -z * w0 + q, r2 = -z * w0 - q;\n              return 1 - (r2 * Math.exp(r1 * t) - r1 * Math.exp(r2 * t)) / (r2 - r1);\n            }\n            // Seeded generator (mulberry32).\n            function rng(seed) {\n              var a = seed >>> 0;\n              return function () {\n                a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n                var t = a;\n                t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n                t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            function onFonts(fn) {\n              if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) document.fonts.ready.then(fn, function () {});\n            }\n            // Sets the group's font size, then shrinks it so the group (or its probe) fits the frame.\n            function fitG(g, size, probe, wf, hf, wmul) {\n              g.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var p = probe || g;\n              var w = Math.max(1, p.offsetWidth * (wmul || 1)), h = Math.max(1, p.offsetHeight);\n              var k = Math.min(1, root.clientWidth * (wf || 0.9) / w, root.clientHeight * (hf || 0.9) / h);\n              if (k < 1) { size = Math.max(6, size * k); g.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n            function fillSizer(sizer, words) {\n              sizer.textContent = \"\";\n              words.forEach(function (w) {\n                var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n                s.textContent = w;\n                sizer.appendChild(s);\n              });\n            }\n            function setText(node, value) {\n              if (node.__t !== value) { node.__t = value; node.textContent = value; }\n            }\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"4\");\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            function start(draw) {\n              var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: Math.round(TOTAL * 30), duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(Math.round(clock.frame * speed * 1000) / 1000); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"word-roller-countdown\"] = tl;\n            }\n\n            \n            var numbers = list(vars.numbers, [\"5\", \"4\", \"3\", \"2\", \"1\"], 10);\n            var N = numbers.length;\n            var finalWord = txt(vars.final_word, \"LAUNCH\");\n            var g = el(\"wcd-g\"), stage = el(\"wcd-clip\"), win = el(\"wcd-win\"), sc = el(\"wcd-sc\"), n0 = el(\"wcd-n0\"), n1 = el(\"wcd-n1\");\n            var fin = el(\"wcd-fin\"), sub = el(\"wcd-sub\"), mt = el(\"wcd-mt\"), mb = el(\"wcd-mb\"), probe = el(\"wcd-probe\");\n            var accent = str(vars.accent, \"#2563eb\"), bgc = str(vars.background, \"#fafafa\");\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--c\", str(vars.color, \"#0a0a0a\"));\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--ac\", accent);\n            fin.textContent = finalWord;\n            probe.textContent = finalWord;\n            sub.textContent = txt(vars.subtitle, \"YOUR JOURNEY BEGINS\");\n            var base = num(vars.font_size, 180, 40, 500);\n            function fit() {\n              g.style.fontSize = base + \"px\";\n              var k = Math.min(1, root.clientWidth * 0.86 / Math.max(1, probe.offsetWidth * 1.2));\n              g.style.fontSize = Math.max(6, base * k) + \"px\";\n            }\n            fit();\n            onFonts(fit);\n            // remocn-scenes: 60 frames counting (12 per number), 15 frames of accelerating blurred spin,\n            // then the final word springs in. The 180 px roller height is 1 em here.\n            function draw(t) {\n              var CD = 60, SD = 15, U = 180;\n              var counting = t < CD, spinning = t >= CD && t < CD + SD, stopping = t >= CD + SD;\n              var scrollY = 0, di = 0;\n              if (counting) {\n                var fpn = CD / N;\n                di = Math.floor(t / fpn);\n                var sp = spring(t % fpn, { damping: 15, stiffness: 200 });\n                scrollY = di + (1 - sp);\n              } else if (spinning) {\n                var s = t - CD;\n                scrollY = N + s * (15 + s * 2) / U;\n              }\n              var urgency = counting ? di / Math.max(1, N - 1) : 1;\n              root.style.background = bgc;\n              mt.style.background = \"linear-gradient(\" + bgc + \", transparent)\";\n              mb.style.background = \"linear-gradient(transparent, \" + bgc + \")\";\n              stage.style.transform = \"scale(\" + (counting ? 1 + 0.02 * Math.sin(t * 0.5) * (1 + urgency) : 1) + \")\";\n              win.style.display = stopping ? \"none\" : \"\";\n              fin.style.display = sub.style.display = stopping ? \"block\" : \"none\";\n              if (!stopping) {\n                if (counting) {\n                  var off = scrollY % 1;\n                  setText(n0, numbers[Math.min(di, N - 1)]);\n                  n0.style.transform = n1.style.transform = \"translateY(\" + (-off) + \"em)\";\n                  n1.style.display = di < N - 1 ? \"\" : \"none\";\n                  if (di < N - 1) setText(n1, numbers[di + 1]);\n                } else {\n                  setText(n0, numbers[Math.floor(scrollY) % N]);\n                  n0.style.transform = \"none\";\n                  n1.style.display = \"none\";\n                }\n                sc.style.filter = spinning ? \"blur(\" + (8 / U) + \"em)\" : \"none\";\n              }\n              var lp = stopping ? spring(t - (CD + SD), { damping: 8, stiffness: 150 }) : 0;\n              fin.style.fontSize = (100 + lp * 20) / U + \"em\";\n              fin.style.transform = \"scale(\" + (1 + lp * 0.1) + \")\";\n              sub.style.opacity = lp;\n            }\n            start(draw);\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
 "sha256": "697ccc932392bc98b7adc53729378a91bbc77832f1da5a29b14f7e48a556b121",
